  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory was generally safety-oriented and ultimately produced executable follow-up, no-self-medication, red-flag, and outpatient/urgent escalation plans. However, there were responsibility-chain defects: the doctor initially overcalled the uncertain local rash as contact dermatitis/allergy, and the initial surgical-conservative concern was never substantively addressed. Under the frozen rubric, any minor/moderate responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite later mitigation and strengths.",
